{"version":1,"slug":"organized__Others__Quantitative_Aptitude__General_Quant__Quantitative_Aptitude_-_General_Quant_-_SSC_SUPER_PRACTICE_41005_(20Q)","path":"organized/Others/Quantitative Aptitude/General Quant/Quantitative Aptitude - General Quant - SSC SUPER PRACTICE 41005 (20Q).html","title":"devgagan","provider":"organized","category":"Others/Quantitative Aptitude/General Quant","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the perimeter of a right angled triangle whose hypotenuse is 6 meters more than twice the shortest side and the third side is 4 meters more than twice the shortest side.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; 6 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2340;&#2368;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379;&#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; 4 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">60 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">60 &#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">70 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">70 &#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">80 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">80 &#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">90 m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">90 &#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Let shortest side = x</p><p> Hypotenuse = 2x + 6</p><p>And third side = 2x + 4</p><p> (2x+6)<sup>2 </sup>= (2x+4)<sup>2</sup> + x<sup>2</sup></p><p>36 + 24x = x<sup>2</sup> + 16 + 16x</p><p>x<sup>2</sup>  -  8x  -  20 = 0</p><p>=&gt; x = 10</p><p>Perimeter = x + 2x + 6 + 2x + 4 = 5x + 10 = 5*10 + 10 = 60</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>At each corner of a triangular field of sides 27 m, 36 m and 45 m a cow is tethered by a rope of length 7 m. Find the area (in m<sup>2</sup>) that cannot be grazed by the cows.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>27 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352;, 36 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; 45 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2366;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; 7 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2352;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2306;&#2343;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2361; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; (&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup> &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2375; &#2327;&#2366;&#2351;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2352; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368;&#2306;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">409</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">409</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">429</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">429</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">449</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">449</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">469</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">469</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>The area of the triangular filed = &#8710;</p><p>= &radic;(s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c))</p><p>Where s = ((a+b+c))/2 = ((27+36+45))/2 = 54 cm</p><p>Therefore &#8710; = &radic;((54)(54-27)(54-36)(54-45))</p><p>&#8710; = &radic;((54)(27)(18)(9)) = 486 sq m</p><p>Area of the field that can be grazed by the cows = 1/2&#960;(7<sup>2</sup>) =22/7 * 7<sup>2</sup>/2 = 77 sq.m</p><p>Therefore area of the field that cannot be grazed = 486  -  77 = 409 sq m.</p><p>Hence the correct option is A.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The circumference of a circular park is 264 m and path of width 12.6 meter running around the park, then what is the area of the path?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; 264 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2323;&#2352; 12.6 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2346;&#2341; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2341; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">3822.29 m<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3822.29 &#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2738.39 m<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2738.39 &#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3325.28 m<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3325.28 &#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">3825.36 m<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">3825.36 &#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>The circumference of a circular park is 264 m<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; 2 * 22/7 * r = 264</p><p>=&gt; r = 42 m</p><p>So, area of the path = 22/7 * (42 + 12.6)<sup>2</sup>  -  22/7 * 42<sup>2</sup> = 22/7 * (54.6<sup>2</sup>  -  42<sup>2</sup>) = 22/7 * 96.6 * 12.6 = 3825.36 m<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The sides of a triangle ABC, AB: BC: CA with base BC, are in the ratio 5: 3: 6. The height of triangle ABC is 4&radic;14 cm. Find the length of CA.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; BC &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABC &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; AB: BC: CA, 5: 3: 6 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABC &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; 4&radic;14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; CA &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">12 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">24 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">15 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">15 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">18 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Let the length of AB = 5X cm, BC = 3X cm and CA = 6X cm respectively.</p><p>Semi-perimeter of triangle = (14X)/2 = 7X cm</p><p>Area of triangle = <img width=331 height=27 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p14097/image001.png\"></p><p>Given Base = 3X cm</p><p>Height = 4&radic;14 cm</p><p>So, 1/2* base* height = 2X<sup>2</sup>* &radic;14</p><p>&frac12;* 3X* 4&radic;14 = 2X<sup>2</sup>* &radic;14</p><p>X = 12/4 = 3</p><p>So, length of CA = 6* 3 = 18 cm.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Areas of two circular fields are in the ratio 1: 4. If the radius of smaller circular field is increased by 80% and the radius of larger circular field is decreased by 40%, then area of the circular field which was smaller earlier will become what percentage of the area of the circular field which was larger earlier?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 1:4 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 80% &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2366; &#2342;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 40% &#2328;&#2335;&#2366; &#2342;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">225%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">225%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">144%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">144%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">100%</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">100%</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">None of these</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2311;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379;&#2312; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Let radii of smaller and larger circular fields are r and R respectively.</p><p>Now, 1: 4 = (&#960;r<sup>2</sup>)/(&#960;R<sup>2</sup>) =&gt; R = 2r</p><p>New radius of field which was smaller earlier = (100 + 80)% of r = 1.8r</p><p>New radius of field which was larger earlier = (100  -  40)% of R = 0.6R = 0.6 * 2r = 1.2r</p><p>Therefore, required percentage = (new area of circular field which was smaller earlier)/(new area of circular field which was larger earlier) * 100</p><p>= (&#960; * 1.8r * 1.8r)/(&#960; * 1.2r * 1.2r) * 100</p><p>= <b>225%</b></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The height of a triangular wall is 3/7 times its base. If the cost of painting the wall is Rs. 30.5 per m<sup>2</sup> is Rs. 1281, then find the height of the wall. </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; 3/7 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2352;&#2306;&#2327;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; 30.5 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 1281 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">6m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">18m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18&#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">10m</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">10 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>The base of a triangular wall = b</p><p>The height of a triangular wall = 3b/7</p><p>Area of the wall = &frac12;  X  b  X  3b/7 = 3b<sup>2</sup>/14</p><p>The cost of painting the wall = 1281 Rs.</p><p>3b<sup>2</sup>/14 = 1281/30.5</p><p>b<sup>2</sup> = 196</p><p>b = 14m</p><p>The height of a triangular wall = 3 X 14/7 = 6m</p><p><sup> </sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>A circular garden of radius 'R' has a drain of 7m around it. If the area of drain around the garden is 462m<sup>2</sup> then find the value of R (in m).</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 'R' &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2327;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2323;&#2352; 7 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2344;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2327;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2323;&#2352; &#2344;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 462 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; R &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; (&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">5</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">14</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2.1</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2.1</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">7</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">7</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Radius of the circular garden = R</p><p>Radius of the circular garden with drain = R + 7</p><p>(Area of circular garden with drain)  -  (Area of circular garden) = 462 m<sup>2</sup></p><p>&#928;(R+7)<sup>2</sup>  -  &#960;R<sup>2</sup> = 462</p><p>22/7 * (R<sup>2</sup> + 49 + 14R  -  R<sup>2</sup>) = 462</p><p>14R + 49 = 21 * 7</p><p>2R + 7 = 21</p><p>2R = 14</p><p>R = 7m</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The perimeter of equilateral triangle and a circle of diameter 21 cm is same. Find the difference between area of the equilateral triangle and circle. (Take &radic;3 = 1.73)</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2324;&#2352; 21 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; (&radic;3 = 1.73 &#2354;&#2375;&#2306;)</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">108.13 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">108.13 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">98.98 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">98.98 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">123.33 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">123.33 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">137.17 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">137.17 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>Radius of circle = 21/2</p><p>Perimeter of circle = 2 * 22/7 * 21/2 = 66 cm</p><p>Area of circle = 22/7 * 21/2 * 21/2 = 346.5 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Perimeter of equilateral triangle = 66 cm</p><p>Side of equilateral triangle = 66/3 = 22 cm</p><p>Area of equilateral triangle = &radic;3/4 * 22 * 22 = 121 *1.73 = 209.33 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Required difference = 346.5  -  209.33 = 137.17 cm<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If the area of the bigger circle is 3773/2 cm<sup>2</sup> and the difference between the circumference of the bigger circle and the smaller circle is 66 cm, then find the area of the smaller circle.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 3773/2 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2324;&#2352; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 66 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">616 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">616 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">346.5 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">346.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">1386 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">1386 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">962.5 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">962.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>The area of the bigger circle = &#960; * radius<sup>2</sup></p><p>3773/2 = 22/ 7 * radius<sup>2</sup></p><p>radius<sup>2</sup> = 600.25</p><p>radius = 24.5</p><p>So, the radius of a bigger circle = 24.5 cm</p><p>Difference between the circumference of the bigger circle and the smaller circle = 66 cm</p><p>2&#960; (24.5  -  radius of a smaller circle) = 66</p><p>24.5  -  radius of a smaller circle = (66 * 7)/ (22 * 2)</p><p>The radius of a smaller circle = 24.5  -  10.5 = 14 cm</p><p>Hence, the area of the smaller circle = &#960; * 14 * 14 = 616 cm<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The sides of a triangle are in the ratio 1/2 : 1/3 : 1/5 and its perimeter is 124 cm. What is the difference (in cm) between the largest and the smallest side?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; 1/2 : 1/3 : 1/5 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 124 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; (&#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">40 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">40 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">28 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">28 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">36 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">44 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">44 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Ratio = 1/2 : 1/3 : 1/5 </p><p>=&gt; 15 : 10 : 6</p><p>Difference between largest and smallest sides</p><p>=&gt; (15  -  6)/(15 + 10 + 6) * 124 = 36 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If the radius of a circle becomes 12 times, then how many times will its circumference become? </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 12 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2368;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">24 times</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">24 &#2348;&#2366;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">144 times</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">144 &#2348;&#2366;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">12 times</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12 &#2348;&#2366;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">6 times</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6 &#2348;&#2366;&#2352;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let the radius be 'r' </p><p>The circumference of the circle = 2&#960;r </p><p>New radius = 12r </p><p>The new circumference = 2&#960;(12r) </p><p>Hence, the required value = [2&#960;*12r]/[2&#960;r]</p><p>= 12 times </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the area of an equilateral triangle whose perimeter is 156 cm.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 156 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">686&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">686&radic;3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">596&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">596&radic;3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">676&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">676&radic;3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">576&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">576&radic;3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>The perimeter of the equilateral triangle is = 3 * Side </p><p>Side = 156/3 = 52 cm</p><p>The area of the equilateral triangle = (&radic;3/4) * Side<sup>2</sup></p><p>= &radic;3/4 * 52 * 52</p><p>= 676&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Find the area of the shaded region.</p><p><img width=169 height=151 id=\"Picture 11\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3789/image026.png\"></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2331;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"169\" height=\"151\" id=\"Picture 11\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3789/image026.png\"></p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">2.58 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2.58 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">16.4 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">16.4 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">19.3 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">19.3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">18.5 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>The triangle is an equilateral triangle.</p><p>We know that, area of equilateral triangle = &radic;3/4 x (side)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= &radic;3/4 x (8)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 16&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 16 x 1.73 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 27.68 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>We know that area of the sector = &#1012;/360 x &#960;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>The triangle is equilateral =&gt; &#1012; = 60<sup>0</sup></p><p>Area of the sectors = 60/360 x 22/7 x 4 x 4</p><p>= 176/21 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 8.38 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Area of three sectors = 8.38 x 3= 25.14</p><p>Area of the shaded region = 27.68  -  25.14 =2.58 cm<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>There is a path around a circular field and ratio of radius of circular field to the width of the path is 4: 1. If area of the path is 346.5 cm<sup>2</sup>, then find the radius of the field?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2323;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 4:1 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 346.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">28 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">28 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">30 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">30 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">14 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">20 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Let radius of the circular field is '4x' cm and width of the path is 'x' cm.</p><p>So, distance of outer line of the path from centre of the field = 4x + x = '5x' cm</p><p>From the question:</p><p>(22/7) * (25x<sup>2</sup>  -  16x<sup>2</sup>) = 346.5</p><p>(22/7) * 9x<sup>2</sup> = 346.5</p><p>x = 3.5</p><p>Radius of the field = 4 * 3.5 = 14 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The area of an isosceles triangle is 32&radic;5 sq. cm, and the ratio of an equal side to the base is 3: 4. Find the perimeter of the isosceles triangle.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 32&radic;5 sq.cm &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 3:4 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">30 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">30 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">20 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">20 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">40 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">40 cm</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">50 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">50 cm</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p><img width=267 height=249 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p16761/image002.png\"></p><p>Height of triangle = &radic;{(3x)<sup>2</sup>  -  (2x)<sup>2</sup>} = x&radic;5</p><p>Area of triangle = &frac12; * (4x)* (x&radic;5) = 32&radic;5</p><p>So, x<sup>2</sup> = 16 => x = 4</p><p>Sides are 12 cm, 12cm and 16cm</p><p>So, perimeter of given triangle = 12 + 12 + 16 = 40 cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The hour hand moves through 6 hours and has a length of 12 cm. Find the area (in sq. cm, rounded off to one decimal place) of the sector covered by the hour hand.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2369;&#2312; 6 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2330;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 12 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2370;&#2312; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (sq. cm &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">226.3</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">226.3</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">221.5</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">221.5</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">229.1</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">229.1</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">232.6</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">232.6</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>We know that one hour of time rotates hour hand by 30&deg;.</p><p>Area covered by the sector = (30* 6/360) * &#960; * (length of hour hand)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= (1/2) * (22/7) * 144</p><p>= 1584/7</p><p>= 226.3 sq. cm</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The area of a triangle is 216 cm<sup>2</sup> and its sides are in the ratio 3 : 4 : 5. The perimeter of the triangle is</p><p></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 216 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 3 : 4 : 5 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2379;, &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2361;&#2376; :</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">&#160;6 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">6 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">&#160;12 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">12 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">&#160;36 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">36 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">&#160;72 cm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">72 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>\"</p><p><span>Let the sides be 3</span><span><i>x</i></span><span>, 4</span><span><i>x</i></span><span>&nbsp;and 5</span><span><i>x</i></span><span>, respectively.</span></p><p><span>Here, (3</span><span><i>x</i></span><span>)</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&nbsp;+ (4</span><span><i>x</i></span><span>)</span><span><sup>2</sup></span><span>&nbsp;= (</span><span>5</span><span>x)</span><span><sup>2</sup></span></p><p>Since, the sides of triangle satisfies</p><p>Pythagoras theorem.</p><p><span></p><p><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005321.png\"/></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span>Triangle is right angled triangle</span></p><p><span><span><img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/a7da26c5055950d6a23c19fc18d41248.png\" />&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></p><p>Perimeter of triangle&nbsp;</p><p><span>=(3</span><span><i>x</i></span><span>&nbsp;+4</span><span><i>x</i></span><span>+ 5</span><span><i>x</i></span><span>)&nbsp;</span><span>c</span><span>m</span></p><p><span>=12</span><span><i>x </i></span><span>cm</span></p><p>=12&nbsp;&#215;&nbsp;6=72cm</p><p>\"</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If the sides of a triangle are 36 cm, 42 cm, and 50 cm, respectively, then find the area of the triangle.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 36 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;, 42 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; 50 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">214&radic;11 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">214&radic;11 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">224&radic;11 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">224&radic;11 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">216&radic;11 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">216&radic;11 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">208&radic;11 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">208&radic;11 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>The sides of a triangle are 36 cm, 42 cm, and 50 cm, respectively.</p><p>S = (16 + 42 + 70)/2 = 64 cm</p><p>Hence, area = &radic;[s(s  -  a)(s  -  b)(s  -  c)] = &radic;[64 * 28 * 22 * 14] = 224&radic;11 cm<sup>2</sup></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The height of an equilateral triangle is 30 cm. find the area of the triangle?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; 30 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">300&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">300&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">400&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">400&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">500&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">500&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup></span>","<span class=\"eqt\">600&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">600&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup></span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Let sides of triangle are 'a' cm</p><p>=&gt; Height = (&radic;3/2) a = 30</p><p>=&gt; a = 60/&radic;3 = 20&radic;3</p><p>=&gt; Area = (&radic;3/4) a<sup>2</sup> = (&radic;3/4) * (20&radic;3) * (20&radic;3) = 300&radic;3 <img width=29 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p18233/image003.png\"></p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>If the circumference is equal to thrice of area of the circle. Find the diameter of the circle.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">4/3 unit</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">4/3 &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">5/4 unit</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">5/4 &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">2/3 unit</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">2/3 &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">&frac34; unit</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&frac34; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>2&#960;r = 3&#960;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>r = 2/3 </p><p>Diameter = 2*2/3 = 4/3 unit</p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}